WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.850
- [Narrator] In North Central Thailand,

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.040
nestled amongst lush green mountain tops,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.000
sits five striking white Buddhas,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.680
in mosaics that glitter
against the landscape.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.263
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.330
Located a five hour drive north of Bangkok

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.700
is Wat Pha Sorn Kaew,

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:21.440
also known as Temple on the Glass Cliff.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.250
This relatively new structure

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.900
was completed in 2004

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.270
and named an official temple in 2010.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.860
The temple features five Buddhas,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.150
all in meditation pose,

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.380
and descending in size,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.520
much like a Russian doll.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.020
They represent the five Buddhas

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:41.129
who visited the earth,
according to Hindu tradition.

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.670
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.840
In addition to the Buddhas,

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.860
this modern structure also includes

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.060
a fivel-level pagoda
shaped like a lotus flower.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.810
The surrounding surfaces are covered with

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.490
around 5 million mosaic tiles, stones,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.380
and pottery, all in vibrant colors.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.190
(upbeat music)

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.150
The site is remote and only accessible

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.180
by private car or tour.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.710
But the journey to this peaceful,

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.044
colorful, modern oasis is
well worth the journey.

00:01:08.044 --> 00:01:10.627
(upbeat music)

